[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":285},["ShallowReactive",2],{"news:\u002Fnews\u002F2013-09-19-new-installation-iso-development":3,"news-timeline":66},{"id":4,"title":5,"author":6,"body":7,"date":56,"description":57,"extension":58,"meta":59,"navigation":60,"path":61,"readingTime":62,"seo":63,"stem":64,"__hash__":65},"news\u002Fnews\u002F2013-09-19-new-installation-iso-development.md","New installation ISO development","cavalier",{"type":8,"value":9,"toc":52},"minimark",[10,14,25,31,34,37,40,45],[11,12,13],"p",{},"As people have started asking if Lunar-Linux were a dead project, we would like to inform you that it is not. Developers are working on improving the Lunar components and new\u002Fupdated modules that hit the Moonbase every week.",[11,15,16,17,24],{},"The next installation ISO has been in development for some time now and there have been 4 development releases on the ",[18,19,23],"a",{"href":20,"rel":21},"http:\u002F\u002Flists.lunar-linux.org\u002Fcgi-bin\u002Fmailman\u002Flistinfo\u002Flunar-dev",[22],"nofollow","lunar-dev"," mailing list.",[11,26,27],{},[28,29,30],"em",{},"What is the current state?",[11,32,33],{},"The ISO got a new build system which makes it more robust to future changes. As this is like starting from scratch, it takes some time to work out all the quirks.",[11,35,36],{},"It will install with systemd and using dracut as init ram disk .You can choose between grub2, lilo and grub as boot loader. The installation ISO is a hybrid, meaning, you can either burn it on an CD\u002FDVD or flash it onto a USB pen drive. The installer will guide you trough the installation process. Setting up font, keyboard, language and time zone. Creating partitions, formatting, mounting and copying the Lunar-Linux system onto it. Configuring the network, adding users and configuring Lunar.",[11,38,39],{},"There are still some things to work out. The ISO doesn't automatically run the guided installer, in the last release the installer need a hot fix to work at all. The generated lilo configuration doesn't boot with dracut. Some files are copied, but shouldn't be there or need to be regenerated.",[11,41,42],{},[28,43,44],{},"What can I do?",[11,46,47,48,51],{},"You can help us with the development by testing or giving us feedback. Just register on the ",[18,49,23],{"href":20,"rel":50},[22]," mailing list test the new ISO releases and report the problems you find.",{"title":53,"searchDepth":54,"depth":54,"links":55},"",3,[],"2013-09-19","The next installer ISO is in development, with a new build system, systemd and dracut.","md",{},true,"\u002Fnews\u002F2013-09-19-new-installation-iso-development",2,{"title":5,"description":57},"news\u002F2013-09-19-new-installation-iso-development","t8trxuHr0DPjCVgXljta5oqwgalxA9f3ad3oEgDcR-k",[67,71,75,79,83,87,91,95,96,100,104,108,111,115,119,123,127,130,134,138,142,146,150,154,158,162,166,170,174,178,182,186,190,194,198,202,206,210,214,218,222,226,230,234,238,242,246,250,254,258,262,266,270,274,277,281],{"title":68,"path":69,"date":70},"Moving towards a more aggressive release cycle","\u002Fnews\u002F2023-08-13-moving-towards-a-more-aggressive-release-cycle","2023-08-13",{"title":72,"path":73,"date":74},"We are moving to libera.chat network","\u002Fnews\u002F2021-05-23-we-are-moving-to-libera-chat-network","2021-05-23",{"title":76,"path":77,"date":78},"We are still very much alive","\u002Fnews\u002F2017-10-18-we-are-still-very-much-alive","2017-10-18",{"title":80,"path":81,"date":82},"Lunar Linux 1.7.0 (i686 & x86_64) ISO’s released","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-10-11-lunar-linux-1-7-0-i686-and-x86-64-isos-released","2014-10-11",{"title":84,"path":85,"date":86},"Lunar Linux 1.7.0-rc2 (i686 & x86_64) ISO’s released","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-09-16-lunar-linux-1-7-0-rc2-i686-and-x86-64-isos-released","2014-09-16",{"title":88,"path":89,"date":90},"Service transition","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-05-24-service-transition","2014-05-24",{"title":92,"path":93,"date":94},"Services from lunar-linux.org may be disrupted",